---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Cosmological Observations Cheat Sheet | Free CMB, Supernovae, BAO"
  description="Complete cosmological observations cheat sheet with CMB, supernovae, and baryon acoustic oscillations. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Cosmological Observations<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>CMB, supernovae, and baryon acoustic oscillations. Evidence for cosmological models.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cosmic Microwave Background</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>CMB Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Temperature: 2.725 K
Blackbody spectrum
Anisotropies: ΔT/T ≈ 10⁻⁵
Recombination at z ≈ 1100
Encodes early universe information</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>CMB Power Spectrum</h3>
        <pre><code>Acoustic peaks: baryon oscillations
Peak positions: angular scale
Peak heights: baryon/photon ratio
Silk damping: small-scale suppression
Lensing: large-scale distortion</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Supernovae</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Type Ia Supernovae</h3>
        <pre><code>Standard candles: fixed luminosity
Phillips relation: brighter = slower
Distance indicator to z ~ 1
Evidence for accelerating expansion
Nobel Prize 2011 (Perlmutter, Riess, Schmidt)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Baryon Acoustic Oscillations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>BAO Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Sound horizon: ~ 150 Mpc
Standard ruler: fixed physical scale
Imprints on galaxy clustering
Measures expansion history
Complementary to CMB</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Large-Scale Structure</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Galaaxy Surveys</h3>
        <pre><code>Sdss, 2dF, DESI, Euclid
Redshift space distortions
Cosmic web: filaments, walls, voids
Growth of structure: fσ₈
Dark energy constraints</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
